  TR['CN-JI-0125'] = {
    "lawId": "CN-JI-0125",
    "sourceLang": "zh",
    "targetLang": "en",
    "engine": "llm",
    "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash",
    "promptVersion": "calr-trans-v2",
    "translatedAt": "2026-10-14",
    "reviewed": "machine",
    "glossaryVersion": "calr-terms-2026-10-v2",
    "completenessNote": "逐条对译，共 1 条；条号与官方原文一一对应，未合并、未省略。",
    "articles": [
      {
        "no": 1,
        "text": {
          "en": "The Supreme People's Court\nLetter in Reply on the Question of the Type of Administrative Case in Which a People's Court\nShould Accept a Case Where a Party, Dissatisfied with a Decision of an Administrative Organ on the Division of a\nState-owned Industrial Enterprise, Institutes Litigation\n27 June 1994      Fa Han No. 34 [1994]\nTo the Higher People's Court of Shanxi Province:\nThe request for instructions of your court, Jin Fa Xing Zi No. 14 [1994], has been received. After study, we are of the opinion that, in accordance with paragraph 2 of Article 2 of the Law of the People's Republic of China on Industrial Enterprises Owned by the Whole People, Article 6 of the Regulations on the Conversion of the Operating Mechanisms of Industrial Enterprises Owned by the Whole People and subparagraph (c) of paragraph 1 of Article 11 of the Administrative Litigation Law of the People's Republic of China, where a party, being dissatisfied with a decision forcibly made by an administrative organ on the division of an industrial enterprise owned by the whole people, institutes administrative litigation with a people's court in accordance with law, the people's court shall accept it as an administrative case of \"infringing the operational autonomy prescribed by law\".\nThis is our reply.\nAttachment:\nThe Higher People's Court of Shanxi Province\nRequest for Instructions and Report on Whether a Case Instituted by a Party\nDissatisfied with a Decision on the Division of an Enterprise Made by an Administrative Organ\nShould Be Accepted as an Administrative Case\n23 April 1994      Jin Fa Xing Zi No. 14 [1994]\nTo the Supreme People's Court:\nThe Yuncheng Prefecture Colour Printing Service General Company of our province, being dissatisfied with the decision on the division of the enterprise made in respect of it by the Commerce Bureau of the Yuncheng Prefecture Administrative Office, instituted administrative litigation with a court. The Yuncheng Prefecture Intermediate People's Court, on 11 January 1994, made a final judgment and, on the ground that the act did not constitute \"an act infringing operational autonomy in respect of which a lawsuit may be instituted with a people's court as prescribed by laws and regulations\", set aside the original first-instance judgment and dismissed the claims of the plaintiff (the facts of the case are set out in the attachment). The Yuncheng Prefecture Colour Printing Service General Company applied to our court for retrial. In the course of the examination, we hold divergent views on whether, where a party institutes a lawsuit out of dissatisfaction with a decision on the division of an enterprise made by an administrative organ, the case should be accepted as a case of infringement of the operational autonomy of the enterprise:\nThe first view is that, in accordance with Article 18 of the Enterprise Law and subparagraph (4) of Article 42 of the Regulations on the Conversion of the Operating Mechanisms of Industrial Enterprises Owned by the Whole People, deciding on the division of an enterprise is the duty of the government and its functional departments, and is an act of organisational restructuring of the enterprises under their jurisdiction carried out by the government in the course of implementing macro-control, which does not fall within the operational autonomy enjoyed by enterprises; even if improper, it cannot constitute an infringement of the operational autonomy of an enterprise; in accordance with Article 47 of the Regulations, correction shall be ordered by the administrative organ at the higher level after a complaint is lodged by the party concerned, and there is no legal basis for a court to accept such a case.\nThe second view is that, in accordance with Article 35 of the Regulations, the government and the relevant departments only enjoy a \"right of approval\" in respect of the division of an enterprise; where the procedure for the division of an enterprise is violated and administrative means are used to forcibly split off a branch of the enterprise, the enterprise will inevitably lose the right to operate and manage part of the State property lawfully acquired by it. Such an act is an act infringing the operational and management rights of an enterprise. Subparagraph (11) of paragraph 1 of Article 47 of the Regulations provides: \"where, without following the statutory procedure and conditions, an enterprise is obstructed or compelled to undergo organisational restructuring\", the government and the relevant departments shall bear the corresponding legal liability. In accordance with paragraph 2 of Article 22 of the Regulations and by reference to Article 37 of the Measures of Shanxi Province for the Implementation of the Conversion of the Operating Mechanisms of Industrial Enterprises Owned by the Whole People formulated by the Shanxi Provincial People's Government, where an enterprise is dissatisfied with such a decision, it may either lodge a complaint with the administrative organ at the higher level or the supervisory department, or directly institute a lawsuit with a court; where a party institutes a lawsuit, the court shall accept it as an administrative case of infringement of the operational autonomy of the enterprise.\nThe administrative division of our court is inclined to the second view. After discussion, the judicial committee of our court is of the opinion that, in view of the fact that this case has a certain impact in society and that the views of the quarters concerned on the issues involved diverge considerably, and for the sake of prudence, a request for instructions is hereby made to the Supreme People's Court for clarification.\nPlease reply whether the foregoing is appropriate."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 1."
        }
      }
    ]
  };

