          "en": "Maritime tort dispute cases:\n(1) cases of dispute over liability for damage arising from the collision of ships, including cases of dispute over liability for damage arising from indirect collision such as wave damage;\n(2) cases of dispute over liability for damage arising from the contact by a ship with facilities or other property at sea, in navigable waters connected to the sea, at ports or on their shores, including cases of dispute over liability for damage arising from the contact by a ship with wharves, breakwaters, trestles, ship locks, bridges, navigation marks, drilling platforms and other facilities;\n(3) cases of dispute over liability for damage arising from damage caused by a ship to facilities erected in the air or laid on the seabed or in navigable waters connected to the sea, or to other property;\n(4) cases of dispute over liability for damage where a ship discharges, leaks or dumps oil, sewage or other harmful substances, causing pollution of waters or loss of other ships, cargo or other property;\n(5) cases of dispute over liability where the navigation or operation of a ship damages fishing or aquaculture facilities or aquaculture products;\n(6) cases of dispute over liability where sunken ships and objects and their wreckage and debris in navigable channels, or temporary or permanent facilities or installations at sea or in navigable waters connected to the sea, affect the navigation of ships and cause loss of ships, cargo and other property and personal injury;\n(7) cases of dispute over liability where the navigation, operation, working or other activities of a ship infringe on the personal rights and interests of others;\n(8) cases of dispute over liability for the unlawful lien on or detention of ships, goods carried on board ships and ship's stores, fuel oil and spares;\n(9) cases of dispute over product quality liability arising from defects in key ship components and special-purpose articles supplied for ship engineering;\n(10) other cases of maritime tort dispute."
